%% Built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/health-and-shutdown.md, section 4). What follows the exit is general/pod_restart_in_place.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Trigger
    participant Infra as InfrastructureSupervisor
    participant Domain as domain supervisor
    participant Children as domain children
    participant InfraChildren as infra children
    participant Broker as Cassini broker
    participant Process as process

    autonumber
    Note over Trigger,Domain: Triggers: health verdict (rejuvenation or hard deadline),<br/>unexpected death of health, router, Cassini client or crypto,<br/>SIGTERM or SIGINT from the kubelet
    Trigger->>Infra: reason
    Note over Infra: begin_shutdown(reason)<br/>log the reason, ignore repeats
    Infra->>InfraChildren: asked about its health from now on, the agent says draining
    Infra->>Infra: start watchdog (the shutdown budget)
    Infra->>InfraChildren: no new signed command is started
    Infra->>Domain: InfrastructureEvent::PrepareShutdown

    Domain->>Children: stop and drain (bounded)
    Children-->>Domain: stopped
    Domain->>Infra: ProceedWithShutdown
    Note over Domain,Infra: A held agent with no work running has nothing to drain, and answers at once

    opt its certificate names an instance: one pod of a multi-instance workload
        Infra->>Broker: Disconnect. No successor of this instance will supersede its session,<br/>which would wait out the retention window as unresponsive
    end
    Note over Infra,Broker: A single-instance workload's session is kept for its successor

    Infra->>InfraChildren: stop (bounded, 10 s)<br/>health, router, tcp client, crypto, and the rest
    InfraChildren-->>Infra: terminated
    Infra-->>Domain: ended
    Domain->>Process: exit non-zero (never 0)
    Note over Domain,Process: The pod's rule restarts all its containers,<br/>and polar-init runs again

    alt domain supervisor never answers
        Note over Infra: watchdog expires
        Infra->>Process: exit 1
    end
